      <Origin>Authored</Origin>
      <ReviewStatus>Current</ReviewStatus>
      <Slot>Example.example:meta-transform-script:round-trip-view</Slot>
      <Title>Round-trip a transform view</Title>
    </DocumentationNarrative>
    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-transform-script:app:narrative:guide:working-with-metatransformscript" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-transform-script:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-transform-script:app:narrative:summary:summary">
      <Body>`MetaTransformScript` understands the supported SQL Server transform surface structurally. It imports views and bounded mutation statements into a typed workspace, then emits equivalent SQL from the same structure.

That workspace gives binding and quality tools access to statements, sources, projections, expressions, predicates, joins, and other supported SQL elements as modeled data.</Body>
